{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve for the product \\(a_1 a_2 a_3\\) where the roots of the equation \\(z^3 = 2 + 2i\\) are \\(a_1 + ib_1, a_2 + ib_2, a_3 + ib_3\\), we start by expressing the right-hand side in polar form. The complex number \\(2 + 2i\\) can be written as:\n\\[2 + 2i = 2\\sqrt{2} \\left( \\cos \\frac{\\pi}{4} + i \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right).\\]\n\nThe cube roots of \\(2 + 2i\\) will be of the form:\n\\[z_k = \\sqrt[3]{2\\sqrt{2}} \\left( \\cos \\left( \\frac{\\frac{\\pi}{4} + 2k\\pi}{3} \\right) + i \\sin \\left( \\frac{\\frac{\\pi}{4} + 2k\\pi}{3} \\right) \\right),\\]\nfor \\(k = 0, 1, 2\\). Here, \\(\\sqrt[3]{2\\sqrt{2}} = \\sqrt[3]{2^{3/2}} = 2^{1/2} = \\sqrt{2}\\), so:\n\\[z_k = \\sqrt{2} \\left( \\cos \\left( \\frac{\\frac{\\pi}{4} + 2k\\pi}{3} \\right) + i \\sin \\left( \\frac{\\frac{\\pi}{4} + 2k\\pi}{3} \\right) \\right).\\]\n\n","prefix_end":768,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,369,279,1985,17767,64,62,16,264,62,17,264,62,18,57758,1380,279,19703,315,279,23606,17767,89,61,18,284,220,17,488,220,17,72,57758,525,17767,64,62,16,488,18668,62,16,11,264,62,17,488,18668,62,17,11,264,62,18,488,18668,62,18,59,701,582,1191,553,36710,279,1290,24413,3108,304,24660,1352,13,576,6351,1372,17767,17,488,220,17,72,57758,646,387,5326,438,510,78045,17,488,220,17,72,284,220,17,59,26888,90,17,92,1124,2359,7,1124,9407,1124,37018,35702,2493,15170,19,92,488,600,1124,15940,1124,37018,35702,2493,15170,19,92,1124,1291,72341,2533,785,23739,19703,315,17767,17,488,220,17,72,57758,686,387,315,279,1352,510,78045,89,4698,284,1124,26888,58,18,15370,17,59,26888,90,17,3417,1124,2359,7,1124,9407,1124,2359,7,1124,37018,35702,37018,35702,2493,15170,19,92,488,220,17,74,59,2493,15170,18,92,1124,1291,8,488,600,1124,15940,1124,2359,7,1124,37018,35702,37018,35702,2493,15170,19,92,488,220,17,74,59,2493,15170,18,92,1124,1291,8,1124,1291,701,59