46,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10061,279,19703,315,198,78045,89,61,18,284,220,17,488,220,17,72,59,60,1371,400,64,62,16,488,18668,62,16,4779,400,64,62,17,488,18668,62,17,4779,323,400,64,62,18,488,18668,62,18,2418,220,22603,400,64,62,16,264,62,17,264,62,18,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet the roots of\n\\[z^3 = 2 + 2i\\]be $a_1 + ib_1,$ $a_2 + ib_2,$ and $a_3 + ib_3.$  Compute $a_1 a_2 a_3.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"ff005de370cff678c70e2b6ba7f332ae5f3edfb147f2e3fb77cf55d8c9c46af5"},"seconds":20.421016931533813,"seed":2730994140769539,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for the product \\(a_1 a_2 a_3\\) where the roots of the equation \\(z^3 = 2 + 2i\\) are \\(a_1 + ib_1, a_2 + ib_2, a_3 + ib_3\\), we start by expressing the right-hand side in polar form. The complex number \\(2 + 2i\\) can be written as:\n\\[2 + 2i = 2\\sqrt{2} \\left( \\cos \\frac{\\pi}{4} + i \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right).\\]\n\nThe cube roots of \\(2 + 2i\\) will be of the form:\n\\[z_k = \\sqrt[3]{2\\sqrt{2}} \\left( \\cos \\left( \\frac{\\frac{\\pi}{4} + 2k\\pi}{3} \\right) + i \\sin \\left( \\frac{\\frac{\\pi}{4} + 2k\\pi}{3} \\right) \\right),\\]\nfor \\(k = 0, 1, 2\\). Here, \\(\\sqrt[3]{2\\sqrt{2}} = \\sqrt[3]{2^{3/2}} = 2^{1/2} = \\sqrt{2}\\), so:\n\\[z_k = \\sqrt{2} \\left( \\cos \\left( \\frac{\\frac{\\pi}{4} + 2k\\pi}{3} \\right) + i \\sin \\left( \\frac{\\frac{\\pi}{4} + 2k\\pi}{3} \\right) \\right).\\]\n\nThe roots are:\n\\[z_0 = \\sqrt{2} \\left( \\cos \\frac{\\pi}{12} + i \\sin \\frac{\\pi}{12} \\right),\\]\n\\[z_1 = \\sqrt{2} \\left( \\cos \\frac{9\\pi}{12} + i \\sin \\frac{9\\pi}{12} \\right) = \\sqrt{2} \\left( \\cos \\frac{3\\pi}{4} + i \\sin \\frac{3\\pi}{4} \\right),\\]\n\\[z_2 = \\sqrt{2} \\left( \\cos \\frac{17\\pi}{12} + i \\sin \\frac{17\\pi}{12} \\right).\\]\n\nThe product of the roots of the polynomial \\(z^3 - (2 + 2i) = 0\\) is the constant term with the sign changed, given by \\(-(2 + 2i)\\). For a polynomial \\(z^3 + az^2 + bz + c = 0\\), the product of the roots is \\(-c\\). Here, the polynomial is \\(z^3 - (2 + 2i) = 0\\), so the product of the roots is \\(2 + 2i\\). Since the roots are \\(a_1 + ib_1, a_2 + ib_2, a_3 + ib_3\\), we have:\n\\[a_1 a_2 a_3 + i b_1 b_2 b_3 = 2 + 2i.\\]\n\nThe real part of the product of the roots is \\(a_1 a_2 a_3\\), and the imaginary part is \\(b_1 b_2 b_3\\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[a_1 a_2 a_3 + i b_1 b_2 b_3 = 2 + 2i.\\]\n\nBy comparing the real parts, we get:\n\\[a_1 a_2 a_3 = 2.\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(a_1 a_2 a_3\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"intermediate_algebra:581"}
